{
	// zappy at full scale, in glass-acid's world. 36 bars, 61.45 s, seven
	// tempos. written after the owner said of glass-acid "this is great,
	// you need zappy on top of this being equally frantic": the same
	// method, the same sound (@acid-draft, the voicing of the tune she
	// kept), and zappy's motif where glass-acid has glass-hour's melody.
	//
	// the plan. the lead is a line of sixteenths on the low d (d2) and
	// its octave. the motif, a d e a | f#, is its loud notes, an octave
	// down at first as glass-hour's tune is in glass-acid. a clock ticks
	// under it and does not change. the tempo steps up into the break
	// and the return is faster again.
	//
	//   1-2   thin, 132 a minute. the line alone on d with gaps, and the
	//         clock. bar 2 ends on e flat, the half step above home.
	//   3-6   hello. the motif as the loud notes, where the ident has
	//         them in its bar (a d e a on beats two to four, the last
	//         note on the next downbeat), an octave down: a3 d4 e4 a4 |
	//         f#4, and under that f# the line drops to b flat, the
	//         ident's floor. again, and this time the last note is f, not
	//         f#: minor, over d.
	//   7-10  build, 136. a kick on every beat, a low bass off the beat,
	//         no gaps in the line. the minor motif and its tail (f e d);
	//         the motif a fourth higher over b flat (d g a d). bar 10:
	//         the kick stops, a snare roll, and the line climbs the scale
	//         two octaves.
	//   11-14 faster, 140 then 144 at bar 13. the motif at double speed
	//         at its own height, one to a bar, each bar starting higher:
	//         from a over d, from c over f, from d over b flat. chord
	//         stabs, the bass rolling. bar 14: the kick doubles and the
	//         line leaps in octaves up to the note that leads home (c#).
	//   15-22 destruction, 148, everything ff. the motif's first three
	//         notes hammered twice a bar, then its last two (a, f) as two
	//         blows of four strikes each, the low note struck between
	//         every one. the same over b flat; moved down for g (g c d |
	//         g e flat); then a, an a major chord hammered, and bar 22
	//         falls down the scale to one low blow half way through.
	//   23-24 the break, 100. the clock alone and the ident, pp, at its
	//         own height, a d e a | f#, four notes and one held. a snare
	//         roll winds up through the second bar.
	//   25-36 return, 152, the fastest, everything ff. the motif at half
	//         speed at its own height over b flat, c and then d major,
	//         where its f# is struck on every beat; its tail (f# e d).
	//         then the motif at speed, twice, over b flat and c each
	//         time. then home: d hammered for two bars, rising to f# and
	//         a; a run up the bright scale from d4 to d6; and one blow.
	//
	// accents: every motif note is f or ff; the filling notes are p in
	// bars 1 to 6, mp in 7 to 9 and under the hammering, mf elsewhere. no slides: the voicing is the
	// one glass-acid was kept with, and it has none.
	//
	// on purpose, against a measurement: in bars 3 to 9 the motif is an
	// octave under where the ident has it, in the 220 to 440 hertz band
	// with the line's low notes, as glass-hour's tune is in glass-acid.
	// that measured as mud and the owner called it great. it is kept.
